QRX 0.0.7.3 Final Release Audit
================================
[1/11] Cross-platform release-plan validation
PASS: linux-x64, linux-arm64, macos-x64, macos-arm64, windows-x64 plans
[2/11] GUI/Core RPC compatibility
QRX GUI/Core compatibility audit: PASS
Validated 29 GUI Core command names against qrx-cli dispatch.
Transport: HTTP JSON-RPC /rpc, network-specific ports 37660-37663.
Wallet session: local PEM verification + qrxd runtime walletpassphrasehex/walletlock parity.
[3/11] Network/RPC security invariants
SECURITY AUDIT: PASS: Core RPC defaults to IPv4 loopback
SECURITY AUDIT: PASS: Non-loopback RPC requires explicit opt-in plus credentials
SECURITY AUDIT: PASS: GUI-managed qrxd explicitly binds RPC to loopback
SECURITY AUDIT: PASS: BTC wallet sidecar is stdin/stdout only; no TCP server listener

Live socket snapshot (Linux):
SECURITY AUDIT: PASS: no live QRX RPC listener detected on 0.0.0.0

Expected design:
  Wallet/Core RPC: 127.0.0.1:37660-37663 only by default.
  BTC Light sidecar: local stdin/stdout process, no inbound TCP listener.
  QRX P2P: separate listener and may use 0.0.0.0 so peers can reach the node.

Remote RPC is an advanced/manual server feature only. It requires:
  --allow-remote-rpc --rpc-user <user> --rpc-password <strong-secret>
and should still be protected by a host firewall/VPN. Do not expose it directly to the Internet.
